-- title:
--   Kodaira–Spencer linearity for re-glued bare deformations
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime, $k := \mathrm{ResidueField}(B)$, $I := \ker(\mathrm{algebraMap}\,B\,B_1)$, and the following data are fixed.
--
--   **Base rings.** $B$ is a commutative artinian local ring with algebraically closed residue field $k$, and $B_1$ is a commutative $B$-algebra such that: `hπ`, the structure map $B \to B_1$ is surjective; `hker`, its kernel $I$ is a nilpotent ideal; `hsmall`, $I \cdot \mathfrak m_B = 0$; `hq`, the image of $q$ in $B$ is nilpotent; and `hI`, $I \subseteq \mathfrak m_B$.
--
--   **The abelian scheme over $B_1$ and its formal group.** $f_1 : A_1 \to \operatorname{Spec} B_1$ is a morphism of schemes carrying a relative group law $L_1$ (a functorial group structure, natural in the base, on the sets of sections of $f_1$ over $\operatorname{Spec} B_1$-schemes), with `hc₁` asserting commutativity of $L_1$ and `h₁` the bundle `AbelianSchemePropertyBundle` for $f_1$, i.e. $f_1$ is smooth and proper, all its fibres are connected, and it admits a relative group law. $F$ is a commutative formal group law in two variables over $B$. The family $\theta_1$ assigns to every $B_1$-algebra $B'$ and every pair $s \in (B')^2$ a section of $f_1$ over $\operatorname{Spec} B'$, and `hθ₁` asserts that $\theta_1$ is a system of formal coordinates for $L_1$ with formal group $F \otimes_B B_1$: it is compatible with $B_1$-algebra maps applied to tuples of nilpotents, and for every $B_1$-algebra $B'$ and ideal $J$ with $J^{n+1} = 0$ it sends $J$-valued tuples to $J$-infinitesimal points, is injective on such tuples, is surjective onto the $J$-infinitesimal points, and transports the $n$-truncated formal group multiplication of $F \otimes_B B_1$ to the multiplication of $L_1$.
--
--   **Torsion and height hypotheses.** `hinf₁`: for every $B_1$-algebra $C$, every $m$ and every section $P$ of $f_1$ over $\operatorname{Spec} C$, if the $q^m$-fold iterated $L_1$-multiple of $P$ is the unit section, then there is a nilpotent ideal $J \subseteq C$ for which $P$ is $J$-infinitesimal. `hheight`: for every field $\kappa$ and every surjective ring homomorphism $\rho : B \to \kappa$, the quotient of $\kappa[[x_1,x_2]]$ by the ideal generated by the components of the $q$-th iterate series of $F \otimes_\rho \kappa$ has $\kappa$-dimension $q^4$.
--
--   **The module $V$.** $V$ is a finite-dimensional $k$-vector space, also a $B$-module compatibly with the $k$-structure and with a central right $k$-action, and $\iota : V \to B$ is an injective $B$-linear map whose image is exactly $I$, viewed as a $B$-submodule.
--
--   **The bare deformation $D_0$ and its chart data.** $D_0$ is a bare deformation of $(f_1, L_1)$ over $B$: a scheme $D_0.A$ with a morphism $D_0.f$ to $\operatorname{Spec} B$, a commutative relative group law $D_0.L$, the abelian-scheme bundle for $D_0.f$, and a morphism $D_0.g : A_1 \to D_0.A$ making $f_1$ the base change of $D_0.f$ along $\operatorname{Spec} B_1 \to \operatorname{Spec} B$ and carrying $L_1$-products to $D_0.L$-products; moreover $D_0.f$ is separated. $\mathcal U$ is an ordered affine cover of $D_0.A$ (a finite linearly ordered index set, affine opens $U_i$ with supremum $\top$), $i_0$ an index, and $e_0 : \operatorname{Spec} B \to U_{i_0}$ a morphism with `he₀`: $e_0$ followed by the open immersion $U_{i_0} \hookrightarrow D_0.A$ is the unit section of $D_0.L$ over the identity of $\operatorname{Spec} B$. Writing $X_k$ for the pullback of $D_0.f$ along $\operatorname{Spec} k \to \operatorname{Spec} B$ and $\mathcal U_k$ for the induced ordered affine cover of $X_k$ (preimages of the $U_i$ under the first projection), $e_1 : \operatorname{Spec} k \to (\mathcal U_k).U\,i_0$ satisfies `he₁`: $e_1$ followed by the open immersion is the unit section of the base-changed group law. For each $s \in \mathcal U.\mathrm{Idx}\,1$, i.e. each strictly increasing pair of indices with associated overlap $\mathcal U.\mathrm{inter}\,s$, $\sigma_s$ is a ring isomorphism $k \otimes_B \Gamma(D_0.A, \mathcal U.\mathrm{inter}\,s) \cong \Gamma(X_k, (\mathcal U_k).\mathrm{inter}\,s)$, with `hσ₁` asserting that $\sigma_s(1 \otimes x)$ is the restriction of the image of $x$ under the first projection, and `hσ₂` that $\sigma_s(a \otimes 1)$ is the image of $a$ under the $k$-algebra structure map.
--
--   **Formal coordinates on $D_0$.** $G_0$ is a deformation of $F \otimes_B B_1$ over $B$, that is a two-dimensional formal group law $G_0.F$ over $B$ reducing to $F \otimes_B B_1$, assumed commutative; $\theta_0$ is a system of formal coordinates for $D_0.f$ with `hθ₀` asserting that $\theta_0$ are formal coordinates for $D_0.L$ with formal group $G_0.F$ in the sense recalled above, and `hl₀` that $\theta_0$ lifts $\theta_1$: for every $B$-algebra $B''$ that is also an $S$-algebra compatibly, and every tuple of nilpotents $s$, the section $\theta_1(B'', s)$ followed by $D_0.g$ equals $\theta_0(B'', s)$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Let $R_0 := \Gamma(X_k, (\mathcal U_k).U\,i_0)$ and let $\mathrm{ev} : R_0 \to k$ be the evaluation homomorphism determined by $e_1$. Let $\mathcal O$ denote the unit $\mathcal O$-module presheaf $U \mapsto \Gamma(X_k, U)$ on $X_k$ relative to the second projection, with its Čech cochain complex for the cover $\mathcal U_k$; write $C^i$ for the cochains in degree $i$ and $H^1 := \ker d^1 / \operatorname{im} d^0$.
--
--   Then there exists a $k$-linear map
--   $$\lambda : \mathrm{Der}_{\mathrm{ev}}\bigl(R_0,\ \mathrm{Hom}_k(V^\vee, H^1)\bigr) \longrightarrow \mathrm{Hom}_k\bigl(V^\vee,\ \text{the first-order deformation space of } F \otimes_B k\bigr),$$
--   where $\mathrm{Der}_{\mathrm{ev}}(R_0, M)$ denotes the $k$-linear maps $R_0 \to M$ satisfying the Leibniz rule $D(ab) = \mathrm{ev}(a)\,D(b) + \mathrm{ev}(b)\,D(a)$, $V^\vee$ is the $k$-dual of $V$, and the first-order deformation space of the reduction $F \otimes_B k$ is the quotient of its first-order cocycles by its first-order coboundaries, such that the following holds for all data as follows.
--
--   Let $c \in \mathrm{Der}_{\mathrm{ev}}\bigl(R_0, \mathrm{Hom}_k(V^\vee, C^1)\bigr)$ satisfy `hc`: $c(a)(\xi) \in \ker d^1$ for all $a \in R_0$ and $\xi \in V^\vee$. Let $\tau$ assign to each $s \in \mathcal U.\mathrm{Idx}\,1$ a self-isomorphism $\tau_s$ of the scheme $\mathcal U.\mathrm{inter}\,s$, subject to `hτ`: for each $s$ there is a function $c_s$ from $R_0$ to $\mathrm{Hom}_k\bigl(V^\vee, k \otimes_B \Gamma(D_0.A, \mathcal U.\mathrm{inter}\,s)\bigr)$ such that, with $C := \Gamma(D_0.A, \mathcal U.\mathrm{inter}\,s)$, the predicate `IsTangentCoordsOfPairAt` holds for the ideal $I$, the module $V$, the map $\iota$, the ring $C$, the two morphisms $\operatorname{Spec} C \to D_0.A$ given by the canonical map of the affine open $\mathcal U.\mathrm{inter}\,s$ and by $\tau_s$ followed by the open immersion, the $k$-scheme $X_k$ with its second projection, the base-changed group law, the first projection, the chart $(\mathcal U_k).U\,i_0$ and the coordinate function $c_s$: that is, there are a morphism $w_0$ from $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the thickening $\bigl(k \otimes_B C\bigr) \otimes_k (k \oplus V)$ to $X_k$ lying over the canonical base morphism, and a lift $w_1$ of its $L_k$-translate into the chart $(\mathcal U_k).U\,i_0$, such that $w_0$ followed by the first projection is a first-order tangent interpolation of the above pair of morphisms, $w_1$ followed by the open immersion is that translate, and $c_s$ is the tangent-coordinate function of the chart ring homomorphism attached to $w_1$; and in addition $\sigma_s\bigl(c_s(a)(\xi)\bigr) = c(a)(\xi)_s$ for all $a \in R_0$, $\xi \in V^\vee$.
--
--   Let $D$ be a bare deformation of $(f_1, L_1)$ over $B$ with `hD`: $D$ is obtained from $D_0$ by re-gluing along $\tau$, i.e. each $\tau_s$ commutes with the structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} B$, each $\tau_s$ fixes the restriction of $D_0.g$ to the overlap, and there are open immersions $U_i \to D.A$ over $D_0.f$ whose images cover $D.A$, compatible with $D_0.g$, and agreeing on overlaps after insertion of $\tau_s$. Let $G$ be a commutative deformation of $F \otimes_B B_1$ over $B$ and $\theta$ a system of formal coordinates for $D.f$ with `hθ`: $\theta$ are formal coordinates for $D.L$ with formal group $G.F$, and `hl`: $\theta$ lifts $\theta_1$. Finally let $u \in \mathrm{Der}_{\mathrm{ev}}\bigl(R_0, \mathrm{Hom}_k(V^\vee, H^1)\bigr)$ satisfy `hu`: for all $a \in R_0$ and $\xi \in V^\vee$ there is a cocycle $z \in \ker d^{0+1}$ equal, as a cochain, to $c(a)(\xi)$ and with $u(a)(\xi)$ the class of $z$ in $H^1$.
--
--   Under these hypotheses, $G$ is the shift of $G_0$ by $\lambda(u)$ in the sense of [`MvFormalGroup.Deformation.IsShiftBy`](def/MvFormalGroup_IsShiftBy.html#L12) for $V$, $\iota$ and $F$: there exist $n \in \mathbb N$, vectors $v_1, \dots, v_n \in V$, first-order cocycles $z_1, \dots, z_n$ for $F \otimes_B k$ and families of power series $zl_i$ over $B$ in the $2 + 2$ variables, such that each $zl_i$ reduces modulo $\mathfrak m_B$ to $z_i$ componentwise, $\lambda(u)(\xi) = \sum_i \xi(v_i)\,[z_i]$ for every $\xi \in V^\vee$, and the defining series of $G.F$ are obtained from those of $G_0.F$ by adding $\sum_i \iota(v_i)\,zl_i$ componentwise.
--
--   The map $\lambda$ is quantified outside all of $c$, $\tau$, $D$, $G$, $\theta$ and $u$: it depends only on the frame $(D_0, \mathcal U, i_0, e_0, e_1, \sigma, G_0, \theta_0)$ and the data of the first six paragraphs.
--
--   This is the linearity statement for the Kodaira–Spencer type correspondence between Čech one-cocycle classes used to re-glue a bare deformation $D_0$ over a small extension and the resulting shift of its formal group law: a single $k$-linear map $\lambda$, depending only on the fixed frame, computes the shift for every admissible re-gluing datum. It is used in the deformation-theoretic step that compares the space of re-gluings with the space of first-order deformations of the formal group, and is cited by [`GoodReductionJacobian.BareDeformation.exists_isFormalCoordinates_liftsCoordinates_of_ker_mul_maximalIdeal_eq_bot`](thm.html#GoodReductionJacobian.BareDeformation.exists_isFormalCoordinates_liftsCoordinates_of_ker_mul_maximalIdeal_eq_bot).
